  General methodology: The global approach considered in this     6143 1451
          work is presented in the following paper: Modern        6143 1451
          nuclear data evaluation with the TALYS code system,     6143 1451
          A.J. Koning and D. Rochman, Nuclear Data Sheets 113     6143 1451
          (2012) 2841.                                            6143 1451
                                                                  6143 1451
  MF2:  Resolved resonance range  (RRR)                           6143 1451
       The RRR was generated with TARES-1.31, compiled on         6143 1451
       12-10-2015 11:58:11 PM at Villingen  , Switzerland. The RRR6143 1451
       expands from 0 to 1.031251E+3 eV. A total of               6143 1451
       2 l-values are used and 200 resonances. The resonance      6143 1451
       formalism is multi-level Breit Wigner (MLBW).              6143 1451
       The ladder approach from the CALENDF code is used to       6143 1451
       generate statistical resonances in the unresolved          6143 1451
       resonance range. Therefore, the URR is translated into     6143 1451
       resolved resonance range. Explanations about the method    6143 1451
       can be found in the CALENDF manual: CEA-Report CEA-R-6277  6143 1451
       "CALENDF-2010: User manual" by J.C. Sublet, P. Ribon and   6143 1451
       M. Coste-Delcaux.                                          6143 1451
       The method of creating statistical resonances in the       6143 1451
       URR region is described in: "From average parameters to    6143 1451
       statistical resolved resonances", D. Rochman et al.,       6143 1451
       Annals of Nucl. Ene. 51 (2013) 60.                         6143 1451
       The s-wave average level spacing is 3.1155 eV and          6143 1451
       the s-wave neutron strength is 0.0004573 1e-4.             6143 1451
                                                                  6143 1451
       After the ladder method, the retroactive method is applied 6143 1451
       to update the MF32 and MF2 with the SAMMY code.            6143 1451
                                                                  6143 1451
  MF32: Covariance file for resonance parameters                  6143 1451
        The compact format is used to represent the covariance    6143 1451
        information on the resonance parameters. Uncertainties    6143 1451
        come from compilations, EXFOR or existing libraries and   6143 1451
        correlations between parameters are obtained following    6143 1451
        the method presented in NIM/A 589 (2008) 85.              6143 1451
        SAMMY is used in the retroactive mode to update MF32.     6143 1451
                                                                  6143 1451
